      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"Ameena\"]\n\nYeah that was what we thought - the cards are in play therefore they would finish resolving even though it&#39;s no longer the Scholar&#39;s Play phase any more.\n\n[/quote]\n\nI agree that this makes sense.&nbsp; Broccoli touched on the idea that it isn&#39;t necessarily Scholar&#39;s turn when DDA gets played, therefore if KWTHF doesn&#39;t stop him from continuing the resolution when it&#39;s Argent&#39;s turn, why would it do so when this happens during his own turn?&nbsp; Also if this were the case, it would mean that the order in which DDA plays were resolved would be hugely significant...you&#39;d always want to have Scholar go last to avoid this risk, and I don&#39;t think it&#39;s consistent with the overall style of SOTM to make it THAT important which order each player does their DDA play in.\n",
